WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
A drip sends fluid straight
into a vein, drop by drop.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.420
A common drip fluid is not pure water.

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.750
It is 0.9 per cent sodium
chloride: salt water.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.660
Pure water seems the
simplest, safest fluid of all.

5
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.900
Yet a drip of it would do harm.

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:22.230
So why would a drip of pure
water into a vein do harm?

7
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.650
In this mission, you'll watch water cross
a membrane that lets water through but

8
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.080
stops sugar.

9
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.490
Then you'll compare cells with
a wall and cells without one,

10
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.550
placed in different solutions.

11
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.770
Your mission: explain why a drip of
pure water into a vein would do harm.
